{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CORRECTION / DISCRIMINATING EVIDENCE for the outlier queue attribution\n\nThe 24–25 minute pre-start waits in the two >50m failures were NOT generic org runner starvation. They were same-change workflow-concurrency blocking under the pre-1792 cancellation bug:\n- 31834162663 and 31834896849 were both Gerrit change 1788. The predecessor ended cancelled at 20:13:07; the 57m successor first started at 20:13:09 after waiting 1,513s.\n- 31840710117 and 31841305299 were both change 1790. The predecessor ended cancelled at 21:35:17; the 50m successor first started at 21:35:18 after waiting 1,453s.\n- Unrelated changes ran concurrently during both intervals, excluding a project-wide serialization explanation.\n\nThus the 57m/50m tail is already addressed by merged change 1792 (4cbaa19315, cancel superseded Verify jobs), subject to its still-open organic replacement proof on esthetic-degrading-pupa. Generic runner contention remains real for aggregate capacity, but it is not the causal attribution of these two initial waits. The current post-fix remaining problem is the ordinary no-queue macOS execution tail, which sampled 29m38s–34m21s end to end in runs 31837971444/31842940708/31843821793."},"env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786747429372460001,"uuid":"37b104d2-b839-4e58-8258-1a9655e50e2d"}